    {
      "id": "node_b3fdad12-aa8a-4d1f-a50c-bc43654bb903",
      "name": "socket_accept",
      "kind": "Processor",
      "parentId": "root",
      "children": [],
      "incomingLinks": [
        "992f1269-5aa2-4929-91a3-5745c23f6cb9",
        "link_47dfe6fa-791b-4863-99ff-002db0ff8f88",
        "link_559f3fef-7b5a-4d0e-9d55-8f70aa5c46b8",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "outgoingLinks": [
        "link_66e6e8e4-5fb1-4171-8bc9-1d22a4323ec5",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "x": 222.32325019058075,
        "y": 1098.441268190992,
        "width": 200.0,
        "height": 138.0,
        "closedWidth": 200.0,
        "closedHeight": 138.0,
        "openWidth": 200.0,
        "openHeight": 138.0,
        "isExpanded": true
      },
      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
      "text": {
        "source": "// Counters that a C body keeps in statics live in the run context.\nsequence, _ := context.Imports[\"socket_accept.sequence\"].(uint64)\nresolvedTotal, _ := context.Imports[\"socket_accept.resolved\"].(uint64)\nlimit, known := context.Imports[\"socket_accept.limit\"].(int64)\nif !known {\n\tlimit, _ = strconv.ParseInt(os.Getenv(\"WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS\"), 10, 64)\n\tcontext.Imports[\"socket_accept.limit\"] = limit\n}\n// Both buffers of the awaitResponseLoop self-link hold the pending copies.\npending := [2]*ThreadworkBuffer{awaitResponseLoop_in, awaitResponseLoop_out}\nvar item ReqRep\n\n// 1. Resolve every response against its pending copy, rotating each loop buffer once.\nfor len(*response) > 0 {\n\tfound := false\n\tif !pop(response, &item) {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"webserver: response buffer holds a value that is not a ReqRep\")\n\t}\n\tfor _, side := range pending {\n\t\tfor remaining := len(*side); remaining > 0; remaining-- {\n\t\t\tvar waiting ReqRep\n\t\t\tif !pop(side, &waiting) {\n\t\t\t\treturn errors.New(\"webserver: pending buffer holds a value that is not a ReqRep\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif found || waiting.id != item.id {\n\t\t\t\tpush(side, waiting)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\tif libhttp.http_resolve(waiting, item) != 0 {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"webserver: client closed the connection early\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif !found {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"webserver: response %s has no pending request\", item.id)\n\t}\n\tresolvedTotal++\n\tif limit > 0 && resolvedTotal >= uint64(limit) {\n\t\tthreadworkRunner.ShutdownRequest()\n\t}\n}\n// 2. Accept at most one connection; wait briefly only when nothing is in flight.\nif threadworkRunner.IsRunning() {\n\ttimeout := 0\n\tif len(*awaitResponseLoop_in) == 0 && len(*awaitResponseLoop_out) == 0 {\n\t\ttimeout = 25\n\t}\n\tif libhttp.http_wait(timeout) {\n\t\tsequence++\n\t\taccepted, status := libhttp.http_accept(sequence)\n\t\tif status < 0 {\n\t\t\treturn errors.New(\"webserver: accepting a connection failed\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tif status > 0 {\n\t\t\tpush(request, accepted)\n\t\t\tpush(awaitResponseLoop_out, accepted)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n} else if len(*awaitResponseLoop_in) == 0 && len(*awaitResponseLoop_out) == 0 {\n\tlibhttp.http_close()\n}\ncontext.Imports[\"socket_accept.sequence\"] = sequence\ncontext.Imports[\"socket_accept.resolved\"] = resolvedTotal",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "port := 8080\nif text := os.Getenv(\"WEBSERVER_PORT\"); text != \"\" {\n\tport, _ = strconv.Atoi(text)\n}\nanyAddress := os.Getenv(\"WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY\") == \"1\"\nif err := libhttp.http_listen(port, anyAddress); err != nil {\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"webserver: cannot listen on port %d\\n\", port)\n\treturn err\n}\nhost := \"127.0.0.1\"\nif anyAddress {\n\thost = \"0.0.0.0\"\n}\nfmt.Printf(\"webserver: listening on http://%s:%d\\n\", host, port)",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "Entry and exit point of every request.\n\nInitialization: read WEBSERVER_PORT and WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY, open the listener with\nlibhttp.http_listen and print \"webserver: listening on http://<address>:<port>\".\nFailure to listen is an error (the process exits non-zero).\n\nEach tick:\n1. Pop every resolved ReqRep from `response` and find its pending copy by id in the\n   awaitResponseLoop self-link. Both of its buffers (awaitResponseLoop_in and\n   awaitResponseLoop_out) are searched by rotating each once, so the copies that do not\n   match keep their order. Resolve the match with libhttp.http_resolve (write the reply,\n   log it, close, free). A response without a pending copy is an error.\n2. While running, accept at most one connection with libhttp.http_accept and push the new\n   ReqRep to both `request` (router) and awaitResponseLoop_out (pending copy). Wait up to\n   25 ms for a connection only when nothing is pending.\n3. Count resolutions; at WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS request shutdown.\nAfter shutdown, stop accepting and close the listener once nothing is pending.",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "- With an unused port, startup prints the listening URL and the process keeps running.\n- With the port already in use, initialization fails and the process exits non-zero.\n- Two concurrent clients receive the responses matching their own requests (ids differ).\n- WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS=1 exits 0 after exactly one access-log line.",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
      "binaryContent": null,
